        uint beforeBalance = address(c).balance;
        uint beforeDeposits = c.depositsCount();

        // Decide whether to act as owner or try to simulate a non-owner call.
        // The InvMutTest contract is the owner of c (per problem statement). To simulate a non-owner caller,
        // we perform the call via address(target) if callerIsOwner==false and target is a contract that will
        // forward the call. However the test harness only runs this run(...) once and msg.sender for calls on c
        // will always be this InvMutTest contract. Therefore to model both cases, we use the boolean:
        // - If callerIsOwner == true: perform the owner-only call directly (this contract is owner).
        // - If callerIsOwner == false: attempt a call that must revert because onlyOwner restricts to owner.
