        // - depositsCount only increases when fallback was invoked (we did one explicit deposit), so afterDeposits >= beforeDeposits
        // - If callerIsOwner, the contract's balance should not increase (owner calls withdraw/sendMoney remove or move funds),
        //   and can only decrease by at most callValue (withdraw transfers that amount) or by callValue if sendMoney forwarded that value.
        // - If not owner, at least one of the owner-only calls should have reverted (we attempted both) and C's balance must remain unchanged.

        assert(
            // deposits monotonicity (we triggered one deposit, so it must be >=)
            afterDeposits >= beforeDeposits
            && (
                callerIsOwner
                ? (
                    // Owner may decrease balance but never increase it by these calls
                    afterBalance <= beforeBalance
